n science, technology, and mathematics. We uphold a commitment to excellence, collaboration, and innovation as we address global challenges and foster a more just and sustainable future. Guided by this mission, SCMNS equips students with the skills, values, and experiences necessary to excel in their careers and make impactful contributions to society.\nNews\nNovember 06, 2026\nThree Morgan State University Faculty Members Earn National and International Fellowships\nOctober 29, 2026\nNIH Awards Morgan State $520,000 Grant to Advance Biomedical Artificial Intelligence Research\nAugust 11, 2026\nScience may finally have made up its mind about coffee\u2019s health benefits \u2013 Doctors used to warn coffee drinkers. Now research reassures them\nAugust 06, 2026\nMaryland Universities Launch AI Degree Programs in Response to Rapid Growth\nMore SCMNS News\nPeer B.E.A.R.S.\nThis program highlights the talent and passion of more experienced SCMNS students to mentor our first-year freshmen through their first two semesters of college, and to increase student engagement and persistence through graduation.\nCONTACT US\nSchool of Computer, Mathematical, and Natural Sciences\nDr. Paul Tchounwou, Dean\nDixon Science Research Center Rm 200\n1700 E. Cold Spring Lane \u2022 Baltimore, MD 21251\nP: 443-885-4515 \u2022 E: scmns-deans-office@morgan.edu\nView on Campus Map\nContact Information\nSchool of Computer, Mathematical, and Natural Sciences\nDr. Paul Tchounwou, Dean\nDixon Science Research Center Rm 200\n1700 E. Cold Spring Lane\nBaltimore, MD 21251\nP: 443-885-4515\nE: scmns-deans-office@morgan.edu\n1700 East Cold Spring Lane\nBaltimore, Maryland 21251\nAPPLY\nADMISSIONS & AID\nSTUDENT LIFE\nSCHEDULE A VISIT\nREQUEST INFORMATION\nGIVE TO MORGAN\nNondiscrimination Notice\nAccessibility\nCareers\nCampus Map\nEmergency Information\nClery Report\nTitle IX Information\nMobile Alerts\nPrivacy\n|\nContact Us\n|\nReport Waste & Fraud\n\u00a9 Morgan State University\nNondiscrimination